  "configuration_id": "config_004",
  "reason": "With only one completed experiment (config_002: multimodal, singleprofile, scvi_n200, imagenet_vit_l, weighted fusion → 53.7% acc, 0.53 GPU hrs), the most important uncertainty is whether multiprofile aggregation adds meaningful value over a single profile. Config_004 is a clean ablation: it keeps the same RNA encoder (scvi_n200), image encoder (imagenet_vit_l), and fusion strategy (weighted) but switches to multiprofile with avgpool aggregation. This isolates the effect of profile aggregation. If it improves accuracy, it justifies further investment in multiprofile+transformer variants; if not, it saves budget by ruling out that direction. Expected relative cost: moderate (~0.7–0.9 GPU hrs), slightly higher than config_002 due to processing multiple profiles, but avgpool is cheap compared to transformer aggregation. This is the best use of experiment 2 because it directly extends the current best result along the highest-impact architectural axis while keeping other variables constant."
}

